{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1148144-archpillars","id":1148144,"title":"ArchPillars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-08T15:51:51-07:00","id":1148144,"title":"ArchPillars","content":"I have seen archmastery be mentioned for pillars and foundations((the system used for dark ages mages/archaic sorcerers)) I would like help to come up with what one could do with arch level pillars for the iterajana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T15:58:29-07:00","id":1148151,"title":"","content":"Have you seen <i>Masters of the Arts</i>?<br /> <br /> Pillars and foundations sounds like you're not dealing with the sphere magick system, but rather stuff from Sorcerer or even another White Wolf game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T16:23:34-07:00","id":1148164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1148144-archpillars?p=1148151#post1148151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen <i>Masters of the Arts</i>?<br /> <br /> Pillars and foundations sounds like you're not dealing with the sphere magick system, but rather stuff from Sorcerer or even another White Wolf game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like OP said, Pillars are what Dark Ages: Mage used. They recently showed up in the Black Hand book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T18:54:37-07:00","id":1148195,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d <i>love</i> to see an archmage writeup for Dark Ages: Mage. The yamasattvas of the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra would be <i>excellent</i> Archaic Sorcerer archmages!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T07:14:52-07:00","id":1148291,"title":"","content":"I would argue that you already have &quot;ArchPillars&quot; to some extent. Depending on how you interpret the rules, and what do you think an Archmaster should be.<br /> <br /> My reasoning takes in count how Archmasters are supposed to reach their level and how Archspheres and Pillars work.<br /> <br /> Archmages are depicted in Masters of the Art as mages that have great curiosity about how things work, the book states that rare it's the archmage that hasn't all the Spheres. Also, they're mages who have &quot;expanded their Paradigms&quot; to be able to hold more and more aspects of the Universe, they're mages who haven't given to the illusion that Mastery of the Spheres covers all that Spheres can do. All of this is fluff, but it's very telling, Archmasters are supposed to think outside the box to discover Archspheres even exist, they're curious, they're depicted learning other Paradigms and adapting them to their own.<br /> <br /> All of this can be represented as Archmages learning new Foundations and Pillars, <i>or even inventing new Pillars and Foundations</i>. Who better to invent a new Pillar or even a new Foundation than one who's depicted as a curious knowledge seeker that's willing to improve their Paradigm going above and beyond Tradition lore? Archmages this way are the ones that trully expand the Paradigm, the creators of the Fellowships, the greatests legends capable of doing things that ordinary Masters would think impossible (because they're hard or even impossible with the 4 Pillars they accept). Isn't that fun?.<br /> <br /> But what about the cosmic powers?. We want cosmic powers!<br /> <br /> Pillar mechanic works in a way that allows them to be better at certain things that Spheres are. Also the combination of two pillars can have more power than any of them alone. Want to create Time Traveling portals or other impossible stuff?, Either combine a Pillar of travel and one of time or create a dedicated Pillar that specializes in time travel. Pillars that are very good at something may be able to do that something earlier than a Sphere would, it stands to reason that the 5th level of a very focused Pillar (or several not so focused ones) could be comparable with a 6th level.<br /> Want to roll twice as many successes as ordinary mages? Combining several Pillars that are good at doing what you want (like causing damage with Vires and Primus) may allow you to increase the multiplier.<br /> <br /> Since not many DA mages can have more than 4 Pillars and 1 Foundations, all of this would be very rare, as it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-09-2017, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T10:51:07-07:00","id":1148361,"title":"","content":"Sort of two questions here. One is, &quot;Why can't I raise my Foundation to 10, like I can Arete?&quot; On this one, remember that Arete is in theory enlightenment and a wider view of the world. Foundation is explicitly not - it is depth, not breadth. A Hermetic who has Modus 5 isn't expanding his mindset to the endless possibilities available; he is only learning to become a better Hermetic. Even if he looks at those &quot;hedge magicians&quot; in other Fellowships, it's likely only so he can design a new Pillar that codifies it in Hermetic terms and opens it to <i>his</i> Order.<br /> <br /> The other question is, &quot;Why can't I raise my Pillars beyond 5?&quot; Here, mostly because I was underwhelmed with the archspheres in <i>Masters of the Art</i>, I'd say that effects beyond the ones listed for the fifth dot just need more successes and rarer components. A 5-dot rating is the maximum understanding of that Pillar of your magical style, and the rest is how you use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T00:45:25-07:00","id":1148540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1148144-archpillars?p=1148164#post1148164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like OP said, Pillars are what Dark Ages: Mage used. They recently showed up in the Black Hand book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Hand book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T00:52:57-07:00","id":1148541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1148144-archpillars?p=1148540#post1148540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black Hand book?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</i>. Released as part of V20. Has a section about ghoul mages that serve the sect, and uses the Foundation/Pillar system for the sake of simplicity (since it's unreasonable to expect Vampire players to go buy M20 just to run a small part of this V20 sourcebook, and the Spheres would take too long to explain for something that would be too broad for the book's purposes anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T08:25:45-07:00","id":1148827,"title":"","content":"both books does mention mages advancing beyond 5 in their pillars by the way that is why i am asking","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T09:43:52-07:00","id":1148843,"title":"","content":"You should first decide if you want to have all 10 levels of MotA, or the &quot;super&quot; 6th level of Horizon. The latter it's easier because it's only 1 level that comes with the promise of being able to do whatever you want within the scope. While the former requires 4 whole levels of stuff you can't do without them (and keeping with the theme).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T17:35:56-07:00","id":1148940,"title":"","content":"This statement is just as relevant to the pillars as the spheres, if not more so.<br /> <br /> I support the existence of Arch Mastery when it is interpreted as a unique form of mastery over a sphere that is personally varied and not quantifiable for all arch-masters of that sphere.<br /> <br /> Because the spheres are in part, a facet of consensual reality, they require that mages know about and believe in them and also that they invoke them, making them manifest in this world, for the spheres to enter into existence and comepltely be real. This statement is derived from various mage sources and is based on my interpretation of canonical sources, not my opinion (though the sources in which I have read this are quite possibly contradicted by other cannon sources)<br /> <br /> Since arch-spheres are not widely understood, nor manifested, they lack the same tangibility in consensual reality (in my opinion).<br /> <br /> Therefore, to me, Arch-spheres are likely to be more tailored to the individual nature of the mage invoking them, more derived from their paradigm and magical style, and thus, more nebulous and difficult to quantify or understand.<br /> <br /> What this means is that arch-spheres will vary from arch-mage to arch-mage in terms of what they can do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}